WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
So I invited a few of the world's best hackers to try to hack me and show me where my vulnerabilities

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.880
are.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.400
And now I'm going to meet them in Las Vegas for DEF CON, the biggest hacker convention

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:09.984
of the year.

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:14.984
They're going to hack me using social engineering, which is essentially hacking without any code.

00:00:14.984 --> 00:00:17.984
They just use a phone and an internet connection.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.499
You wanna do a sample vishing call?

00:00:19.499 --> 00:00:20.499
What's vishing?

00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:24.648
Vishing is voice elicitation, and basically what you do is you use the phone

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:29.728
to extract information or data points that can be used in a later attack.

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:31.953
Let's do it. Who are you going to call?

00:00:31.953 --> 00:00:37.953
Maybe I'll call your cell phone provider and see if I can get them to give me your email address.

00:00:37.953 --> 00:00:39.937
I bet they're good. I bet they have my back.

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:45.737
But yeah, go for it. I'm going to spoof from your number, so it's going to look like it's calling from you. Okay.

00:00:48.357 --> 00:00:49.922
Hi, I'm actually, I'm so sorry.

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:51.922
Can you hear me okay?

00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:53.922
My baby, I'm sorry.

00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:57.922
My husband's like, "We're about to apply for a loan,

00:00:57.922 --> 00:00:59.907
and we just had a baby," and he's like, "Get this

00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:05.707
done by today." So I'm so sorry, I can't call you back. I'm trying to log into our

00:01:05.707 --> 00:01:09.891
account for user information, and I can't remember what email

00:01:09.891 --> 00:01:16.891
address we used to log the account in. The baby's crying, and, um, can you help me?

00:01:16.891 --> 00:01:17.891
Awesome.

00:01:17.891 --> 00:01:19.876
In just 30 seconds,

00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:22.876
Jessica gets access to my personal email address.

00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:27.876
Now if I needed to add our daughter on our account so she could call in and make changes,

00:01:27.876 --> 00:01:29.860
how would I need to go about doing that?

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:35.620
You would have to send me a secure PIN through a text message? Yeah. Well, the thing is, I don't think I'll be able to receive

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.620
a text message if I'm on the phone. Oh,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.845
I'm not on there either?

00:01:41.845 --> 00:01:45.845
So I thought when we got married, he added me to the account.

00:01:45.845 --> 00:01:49.829
Jess uses my girlfriend's name and a fake Social Security number

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:53.069
to set up her own personal access to my account.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:55.309
Wait, I'm sorry, so there's no password on my account right now?

00:01:55.309 --> 00:01:56.469
Can I set that up?

00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:59.189
She even gets the support person to change my password.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.414
Thank you so much for your help today. So she just basically blocked me out of my own

00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:06.500
account. I'll get her fed after this.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.174
All right, thank you.
